    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40044" root="نظر" body-key="n">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِظْرٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَظِيرٌ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  A man says to another,
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَيْعٌ</span>, [or perhaps <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِيعٌ</span>, like the word used in
reply to it. here following and like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خِطْبٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِكْحٌ</span> meaning, I sell and the other says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نِظْرٌ</span>,
meaning, <i>Grant me a delay</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْظِرْنِى</span>) that I
may buy (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْتَرِى</span>) of thee. (M, TA.)

